<style>
    code {
        color: var(--sayori-orange);
    }

    h2 {
        font-family: "Caveat Brush", 'Franklin Gothic Medium', 'Arial Narrow', Arial, sans-serif;
    }
</style>

<main class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-5 py-24">
    <section class="text-center mb-16">
        <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-[var(--sayori-orange)] text-sm">
            Community
        </p>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-[clamp(3rem,8vw,5rem)] mt-4">
            Feedback & Suggestions
        </h1>
        <p class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-6 leading-8 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
            Every great game starts with an idea. Whether you've found a bug,
            have a feature request, or simply want to share your thoughts,
            we'd love to hear them.
        </p>
        <a href="https://forms.gle/w36x89tjFFxE32rY8"
            class="inline-block mt-8 rounded-full bg-[var(--sayori-orange)] text-black font-semibold px-8 py-3 transition hover:scale-105">
            Open Feedback Form
        </a>
    </section>
    <section class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="rounded-3xl border border-[var(--sayori-border)] bg-[var(--sayori-surface)] p-8">
            <div class="text-4xl">
                💡
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-5">
                Suggest Something
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 leading-8 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
                Have an idea for a new game? Want a new command? Think Sayori could do something cooler? We'd love to
                hear it. So, drop it and we will see if we can make it a success or not.
            </p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-3xl border border-[var(--sayori-border)] bg-[var(--sayori-surface)] p-8">
            <div class="text-4xl">
                🐞
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-5">
                Report a Bug
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 leading-8 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
                Something not working correctly? Commands behaving strangely? Tell us what happened so we can
                investigate and solve the issue for you.
            </p>
        </article>
    </section>
    <section class="mt-16 rounded-3xl border border-[var(--sayori-border)] bg-[var(--sayori-surface)] p-8">
        <h2 class="text-3xl">
            Before You Submit a bug or a complain.
        </h2>
        <ul class="mt-8 space-y-4 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
            <li>✔ Mention the command involved.</li>
            <li>✔ Tell us what you expected to happen.</li>
            <li>✔ Tell us what actually happened.</li>
            <li>✔ More details = easier to reproduce.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-4xl">
            What Happens Next?
        </h2>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3 mt-10">
            <article class="rounded-3xl p-8 border border-[var(--sayori-border)] bg-[var(--sayori-surface)]">
                <div class="text-4xl">📨</div>
                <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-5">
                    Submitted
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--sayori-muted)] leading-7">
                    Your response have reached to us.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="rounded-3xl p-8 border border-[var(--sayori-border)] bg-[var(--sayori-surface)]">
                <div class="text-4xl">🔍</div>
                <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-5">
                    Reviewed
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--sayori-muted)] leading-7">
                    We look into the response and assign the task to designated person on the team.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="rounded-3xl p-8 border border-[var(--sayori-border)] bg-[var(--sayori-surface)]">
                <div class="text-4xl">🚀</div>
                <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-5">
                    Action
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--sayori-muted)] leading-7">
                    Investigate and fix the bugs. Code and complete the new requests.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl">
            Frequently Asked Questions
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-10 space-y-4">
            <article class="faq-item">
                <button class="faq-question">
                    <span>
                        Will every suggestion be added?
                    </span>
                    <span class="faq-arrow">&gt;</span>
                </button>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    <p>
                        We try to fit in most of the ideas, but if the idea doesn't fit the vision we have for Sayori,
                        then we try to improve to see if it fits or not.
                        <br> When ideas fit, they are adapted as soon ans possible, and if they don't we will inform
                        you, so you don't feel disappointed.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="faq-item">
                <button class="faq-question">
                    <span>
                        Can I submit multiple suggestions?
                    </span>
                    <span class="faq-arrow">&gt;</span>
                </button>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    <p>
                        Absolutely. The more the merrier. Do not hold back. <br>
                        Try to not mix multiple ideas or feedbacks in a single form, it makes it harder to understand
                        what comment is being passed for what feature.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="faq-item">
                <button class="faq-question">
                    <span>
                        Will I receive a reply?
                    </span>
                    <span class="faq-arrow">&gt;</span>
                </button>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    <p>
                        Not necessarily, but every submission is read. If you are too curious to know if we have read
                        the feedback or suggestion you sent via the form, you can use the <code>/feedback</code> command
                        as well, or reach out to the developers via the official server.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="text-center mt-20">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl">
            Thank You ❤️
        </h2>
        <p class="max-w-2xl mx-auto mt-6 leading-8 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
            Every feature begins as someone's idea. <br> Even if your suggestion isn't implemented, your feedback helps
            make Sayori better.
        </p>
        <p class="max-w-2xl mx-auto mt-6 leading-8 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
            We genuinely care for the support you show us.
        </p>
    </section>
</main>

<script>
    const faqItems = document.querySelectorAll(".faq-item");
    faqItems.forEach(item => {
        item.querySelector(".faq-question").addEventListener("click", () => {
            const isOpen = item.classList.contains("active");
            faqItems.forEach(faq => {
                faq.classList.remove("active");
            });
            if (!isOpen) {
                item.classList.add("active");
            }
        });
    });
</script>